<item>
            <title>[LU-20763] Nodemap fileset removal declares 256 index deletes per fileset</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20763</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Removing a nodemap fileset wipes the whole subid range reserved for that fileset instead of deleting the records the fileset actually occupies. Every fileset removal therefore declares LUSTRE_NODEMAP_FILESET_SUBID_RANGE (256) index deletes in a single transaction, whatever the length of the fileset path, and even when the nodemap has no fileset at all.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On ldiskfs each osd_index_declare_iam_delete() charges osd_dto_credits_noquota&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;DTO_INDEX_DELETE&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; (1) + 3 = 4 credits, so one removal declares 1024 credits. When that exceeds the maximum transaction size of the journal, osd_trans_start() clamps the transaction down to jbd2_journal_get_max_txn_bufs(journal) / 2 and osd_trans_exec_op() reports the mismatch:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;  lustre-MDT0000: opcode 9: before 516 &amp;lt; left 1024, rollback = 8
    create: 0/0/0, destroy: 0/0/0
    attr_set: 0/0/0, xattr_set: 1/1/0
    write: 0/0/0, punch: 0/0/0, quota 1/3/0
    insert: 0/0/0, delete: 256/1024/0
    ref_add: 0/0/0, ref_del: 0/0/0
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
